Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; GTA2 RTX Remix renderer - registry setup.
;
; GTA2 loads two DLLs by name from this key: the renderer and the video device.
; Pointing both at our own file names is what lets the mod install by unzipping,
; without overwriting anything of the game's.
;
;   rendername   the renderer. gta2dx9.dll is ours.
;   videoname    the video device, which owns the screen. gta2dx9_vid.dll is
;                ours and forwards everything it does not handle to the game's
;                own Dmavideo.dll, which is left exactly where it is.
;   lighting     GTA2 only builds its light list when this is set. With it clear
;                the game never calls gbh_AddLight and there is nothing for the
;                path tracer to light the city with.
;   max/min_frame_rate  GTA2's own frame cap, which is a boolean and not a
;                number: on means 30 fps. Off here because the renderer caps the
;                frame itself, and its cap is a real number - see fps_cap in
;                gta2dx9.ini.
;
; Both hives are written. The GTA2 manager and the in-game options screen write
; HKLM, and the game has been seen reading either.
;
; Your own resolution settings are deliberately not touched.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\WOW6432Node\DMA Design Ltd\GTA2\Screen]
"rendername"="gta2dx9.dll"
"videoname"="gta2dx9_vid.dll"
"lighting"=dword:00000001
"max_frame_rate"=dword:00000000
"min_frame_rate"=dword:00000000

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\SOFTWARE\DMA Design Ltd\GTA2\Screen]
"rendername"="gta2dx9.dll"
"videoname"="gta2dx9_vid.dll"
"lighting"=dword:00000001
"max_frame_rate"=dword:00000000
"min_frame_rate"=dword:00000000
